<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Harar</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Harar is a walled city in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>, a centre of Islamic learning and trade. It became the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adal-sultanate">Adal Sultanate</a> and the base for campaigns against the Christian Ethiopian state. Its walls were built after the Adal wars, and the city remained a leading centre of the region after the sultanate's decline.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/harar.jpg" alt="Harar" width="320" height="390" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rod Waddington from Kergunyah, Australia · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:City_Gate,_Harar_Jugol_(14464345823).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
